From e86c5c8aebf3533737e8b246d60e5aaa7fdee2aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RA8D1 port <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 13:54:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] boards: ek_ra8d1: use a single GLCDC frame buffer

With two frame buffers, display_renesas_ra.c takes the buffer-change
path, sets vsync_wait and blocks on k_sem_take(frame_buf_sem, K_FOREVER).
That semaphore is only given by the GLCDC line-detect interrupt, which
does not fire on this board, so the main thread blocks forever on the
first displayio refresh.

The failure is silent and total: the boot banner reaches the panel
because the first buffer change lands before the wait, then the console,
USB servicing, code.py and the REPL all stop together.

A single frame buffer avoids the buffer-change path. The alternative fix
is to bound the wait in the driver.
---
 ports/zephyr-cp/boards/ek_ra8d1.conf | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ports/zephyr-cp/boards/ek_ra8d1.conf b/ports/zephyr-cp/boards/ek_ra8d1.conf
index 451f41991..2e7b463f3 100644
--- a/ports/zephyr-cp/boards/ek_ra8d1.conf
+++ b/ports/zephyr-cp/boards/ek_ra8d1.conf
@@ -10,3 +10,8 @@ CONFIG_USBD_MAX_UDC_MSG=32
 CONFIG_USBD_MSG_SLAB_COUNT=32
 CONFIG_UDC_BUF_COUNT=32
 CONFIG_UDC_BUF_POOL_SIZE=2048
+
+# FIX-GLCDC-FBNUM: GLCDC line-detect IRQ never fires, so ra_display_write blocks
+# forever on k_sem_take(frame_buf_sem, K_FOREVER) at display_renesas_ra.c:146.
+# Single frame buffer avoids the buffer-change path that sets vsync_wait.
+CONFIG_RENESAS_RA_GLCDC_FB_NUM=1
